#. command help: didact about
#: didact/commands/knowledge.py
msgid ""
"Details are short named notes for whoever runs the game; keep them current and the\n"
"game stays consistent. Suggested names depend on the record (looks, personality,\n"
"wants, fears, attitude, doing, plan, where, history, powers, state, secret,\n"
"thoughts); any one-word name works. `thoughts` is for your own ideas about what you\n"
"made. Players see only `looks`; `reveal <record> <name>` shows them another.\n"
"Without values: the details, the suggestions still open, the record's chronicle\n"
"(journal beats `--about` it), what it holds and where it is. This view is for the GM."
msgstr ""
"Detaljer er korte, navngivne noter til den, der leder spillet; hold dem ajour, så\n"
"forbliver spillet konsistent. Foreslåede navne afhænger af opslaget (looks, personality,\n"
"wants, fears, attitude, doing, plan, where, history, powers, state, secret,\n"
"thoughts); ethvert navn på ét ord virker. `thoughts` er til dine egne idéer om det, du\n"
"har skabt. Spillerne ser kun `looks`; `reveal <record> <name>` viser dem en anden.\n"
"Uden værdier: detaljerne, de forslag, der stadig er åbne, opslagets krønike\n"
"(journalbegivenheder med `--about` om det), hvad det rummer, og hvor det er. Denne visning er til"
" SL."

