#. command help: didact reset
#: didact/commands/care.py
msgid "Empty the library, as if Didact were newly installed (shown first; backed up first)"
msgstr "Tøm biblioteket, som om Didact lige var installeret (vises først; sikkerhedskopieres først)"

#: didact/web/pages/library.py
msgid ""
"Empty the library, as if Didact were newly installed: every world, campaign and change goes, and "
"numbering starts again at #e1. A backup is made first, and backups stay."
msgstr ""
"Tøm biblioteket, som om Didact lige var installeret: alle verdener, kampagner og ændringer "
"forsvinder, og nummereringen starter forfra ved #e1. Der tages en sikkerhedskopi først, og "
"sikkerhedskopierne bliver."

#: didact/web/pages/library.py
msgid "Enable"
msgstr "Aktivér"

#: didact/web/pages/library.py
msgid ""
"Enabling a pack adds it to the open campaign. The core pack is always on, and one game system is "
"in use at a time: the open world's, which it keeps for good."
msgstr ""
"Når du aktiverer en pakke, føjes den til den åbne kampagne. Kernepakken er altid slået til, og "
"der er kun ét spilsystem i brug ad gangen: den åbne verdens, som den beholder for altid."

#: didact/web/pages/overview.py
msgid "End session"
msgstr "Afslut spilgang"

#. command help: didact scene end
#: didact/commands/play.py
msgid "End the current scene (optionally with its summary)"
msgstr "Afslut den aktuelle scene (eventuelt med dens resumé)"

#. command help: didact combat end
#: didact/commands/combat.py
msgid "End the fight"
msgstr "Afslut kampen"

#. command help: didact session end
#: didact/commands/play.py
msgid "End the session (give its summary now, or later with `summary write session`)"
msgstr "Afslut spilgangen (giv dens resumé nu, eller senere med `summary write session`)"

#: didact/web/pages/library.py
msgid ""
"Every change, newest first. Undo takes the last one back, or pick one; jump back to a change to "
"take back everything after it."
msgstr ""
"Alle ændringer, nyeste først. Fortryd tager den seneste tilbage, eller vælg en; spring tilbage "
"til en ændring for at tage alt efter den tilbage."

#. command help: didact faction turn
#: didact/commands/tracking.py
msgid ""
"Every faction that isn't gone takes a turn: the system's `settings.factions.turn`\n"
"rule, or a roll (d6; 4+ ticks each of its clocks: `track new … --for faction:x`).\n"
"Narrate the moves from their agendas. Secret factions act too; `--gm` shows them."
msgstr ""
"Hver fraktion, der ikke er forsvundet, tager en tur: systemets regel `settings.factions.turn`\n"
"eller et slag (d6; 4+ rykker hvert af dens ure: `track new … --for faction:x`).\n"
"Fortæl trækkene ud fra deres dagsordener. Hemmelige fraktioner handler også; `--gm` viser dem."

#: didact/web/pages/settings.py
msgid "Every module's documentation, from its docstrings and types."
msgstr "Dokumentationen for hvert modul, ud fra dets docstrings og typer."

#. command help: didact gen run
#: didact/commands/drafts.py
msgid ""
"Every roll is logged. `--prefill` gives decisions in advance (a choice takes the\n"
"option it names; a list gives one value per occurrence); `--auto` lets the dice make\n"
"the choices the procedure would otherwise ask about. Then `gen show`, `gen edit`,\n"
"`gen commit`."
msgstr ""
"Hvert slag logges. `--prefill` giver beslutninger på forhånd (et valg får den mulighed,\n"
"der nævnes; en liste giver én værdi pr. forekomst); `--auto` lader terningerne træffe de\n"
"valg, proceduren ellers ville spørge om. Derefter `gen show`, `gen edit`, `gen commit`."

#: didact/web/pages/graph.py
msgid "Every type is switched off: turn one on above."
msgstr "Alle typer er slået fra: slå en til ovenfor."

#. command help: didact reset
#: didact/commands/care.py
msgid ""
"Every world, campaign and record goes, with the history, drafts, save points and the\n"
"search index, and numbering starts again: the next change is #e1, the next roll #r1.\n"
"The backups stay, and so do installed packs unless --packs. The library as it is is\n"
"backed up first (snapshot-<time>-before-reset.zip): undo can't take a reset back, but\n"
"restoring that backup can. Without --yes it only shows what would go."
msgstr ""
"Alle verdener, kampagner og opslag forsvinder, med historikken, kladderne, gemmepunkterne og\n"
"søgeindekset, og nummereringen starter forfra: den næste ændring er #e1, det næste slag #r1.\n"
"Sikkerhedskopierne bliver, og det samme gør installerede pakker, medmindre --packs. Biblioteket, "
"som det er, bliver\n"
"sikkerhedskopieret først (snapshot-<time>-before-reset.zip): fortryd kan ikke tage en nulstilling"
" tilbage, men\n"
"at gendanne den sikkerhedskopi kan. Uden --yes viser den kun, hvad der ville forsvinde."

#: didact/web/pages/library.py
msgid ""
"Everything after it is taken back, newest first: each change is undone, and each roll is marked "
"undone. Nothing is deleted: Redo, or jumping back to a later change, brings it back."
msgstr ""
"Alt efter den tages tilbage, nyeste først: hver ændring fortrydes, og hvert slag markeres som "
"fortrudt. Intet slettes: Gentag, eller at springe tilbage til en senere ændring, bringer det "
"tilbage."

#: didact/web/pages/library.py
msgid "Everything but the newest ones you keep goes for good: this can't be undone."
msgstr "Alt undtagen de nyeste, du beholder, forsvinder for altid: det kan ikke fortrydes."

#: didact/web/pages/library.py
msgid ""
"Everything in the library but its backups is replaced by the backup's. The library as it is now "
"is backed up first: undo can't take a restore back, but restoring that backup can."
msgstr ""
"Alt i biblioteket undtagen sikkerhedskopierne erstattes af sikkerhedskopiens indhold. "
"Biblioteket, som det er nu, sikkerhedskopieres først: fortryd kan ikke tage en gendannelse "
"tilbage, men det kan en gendannelse af den sikkerhedskopi."

#. command help: didact world delete
#: didact/commands/library.py
msgid ""
"Everything in the world goes: its records, maps, lore and every campaign in it\n"
"(sessions, journals, transcripts, oracle state). Without --yes it shows what would\n"
"go and stages the change for `didact apply <id>`. `didact undo` brings it all back,\n"
"byte for byte. The event log keeps its history either way."
msgstr ""
"Alt i verdenen forsvinder: dens opslag, kort, lore og alle kampagner i den\n"
"(spilgange, journaler, transskripter, orakeltilstand). Uden --yes viser den, hvad der ville\n"
"forsvinde, og forbereder ændringen til `didact apply <id>`. `didact undo` bringer det hele "
"tilbage,\n"
"byte for byte. Hændelsesloggen bevarer sin historik under alle omstændigheder."

