#. command help: didact pack enable
#: didact/commands/packs.py
msgid ""
"One game system is in use at a time: the open world's. A world keeps the system it\n"
"was made with, so enabling a system only gives one to a world that has none yet;\n"
"another system plays in a world of its own (`didact world new <id> --system <pack>`).\n"
"A pack that needs another system (a setting written for it) can't be added either."
msgstr ""
"Der er kun ét spilsystem i brug ad gangen: den åbne verdens. En verden beholder det system,\n"
"den blev oprettet med, så at aktivere et system giver kun et til en verden, der ikke har et "
"endnu;\n"
"et andet system spilles i sin egen verden (`didact world new <id> --system <pack>`).\n"
"En pakke, der kræver et andet system (en spilverden skrevet til det), kan heller ikke tilføjes."

#. command help: didact search
#: didact/commands/reference.py
msgid ""
"One ranked list across every source (every word must appear; titles count most).\n"
"Each hit ends with the command that shows it. Records follow player-safe rules\n"
"unless you pass --gm. Sources: rules, terms, mechanics, tables, compendium, records,\n"
"transcript, docs."
msgstr ""
"Én rangeret liste på tværs af alle kilder (hvert ord skal forekomme; titler tæller mest).\n"
"Hvert fund slutter med den kommando, der viser det. Opslag følger reglerne for, hvad spillerne må"
" se,\n"
"medmindre du angiver --gm. Kilder: rules, terms, mechanics, tables, compendium, records,\n"
"transcript, docs."

