"{count} af dem bliver."

#. command help: didact snapshot
#: didact/commands/care.py
msgid ""
"Zips the whole data home (all but its backups) into backups/. Ending a session\n"
"makes one too (snapshot-<time>-auto.zip), and only the newest five of those stay.\n"
"\n"
"--restore shows what a backup holds next to the library now. With --yes it backs\n"
"the library up as it is (snapshot-<time>-before-restore.zip), then puts the\n"
"backup's files in place of everything but the backups. Undo can't take a restore\n"
"back: restoring that backup can. Event and roll numbers carry on.\n"
"\n"
"--remove and --keep delete backups for good: they aren't part of the library's\n"
"history, so undo can't bring them back."
msgstr ""
"Zipper hele datamappen (alt undtagen dens sikkerhedskopier) ind i backups/. At afslutte en "
"spilgang\n"
"laver også én (snapshot-<time>-auto.zip), og kun de fem nyeste af dem bliver.\n"
"\n"
"--restore viser, hvad en sikkerhedskopi rummer, ved siden af biblioteket nu. Med --yes\n"
"sikkerhedskopierer den biblioteket, som det er (snapshot-<time>-before-restore.zip), og sætter "
"derefter\n"
"sikkerhedskopiens filer i stedet for alt undtagen sikkerhedskopierne. Fortryd kan ikke tage en "
"gendannelse\n"
"tilbage: at gendanne den sikkerhedskopi kan. Hændelses- og slagnumre fortsætter.\n"
"\n"
"--remove og --keep sletter sikkerhedskopier for altid: de er ikke en del af bibliotekets\n"
"historik, så fortryd kan ikke bringe dem tilbage."

